      "math_academy_id": "e-14089",
      "problem": "In an inverse variation, $y=5$ when $x=8.$ Find an equation that relates $x$ and $y.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $y$ varies inversely with $x,$ we use the equation\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{k}{x}.\n$$\n\nNext, we use the data $y=5$ when $x=8$ to find $k\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =\\frac{k}{8} \\\\ 5\\cdot 8 & =k \\\\ 40 & =k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our inverse variation equation is\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac{40}{x}.\n$$",
